{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03292",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 5.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Hi doctor, you know, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.91,
      "end_seconds": 10.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.55,
      "end_seconds": 19.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.51,
      "end_seconds": 25.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Alright, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.52,
      "end_seconds": 33.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "Oh, doctor, it's bloating when I slip up. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.37,
      "end_seconds": 38.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.98,
      "end_seconds": 52.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "Okay, so about... well, two weeks. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.11,
      "end_seconds": 59.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.0,
      "end_seconds": 71.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Yes, gluten. That makes it worse. Only avoiding gluten, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.17,
      "end_seconds": 74.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.57,
      "end_seconds": 98.69,
      "duration_seconds": 22.12,
      "text": "Mouth ulcers goes along with it, you know, most of the time. Right, um, the mouth ulcers? That's been since Monday. Okay, you know, so as for mouth ulcers, a three out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.68,
      "end_seconds": 103.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Have you had bone pain, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.36,
      "end_seconds": 106.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Nope, no bone pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.88,
      "end_seconds": 112.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, diarrhoea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.74,
      "end_seconds": 118.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "No, no weight loss, diarrhoea or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.96,
      "end_seconds": 122.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.03,
      "end_seconds": 126.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Right, I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.19,
      "end_seconds": 135.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Yeah, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.26,
      "end_seconds": 141.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.13,
      "end_seconds": 153.08,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.1,
      "end_seconds": 158.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.64,
      "end_seconds": 162.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.55,
      "end_seconds": 167.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.96,
      "end_seconds": 176.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "I mean, just a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.68,
      "end_seconds": 181.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.69,
      "end_seconds": 183.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.18,
      "end_seconds": 197.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.33,
      "end_seconds": 206.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "I have anxiety. Mm, I've had an irregular heartbeat for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.22,
      "end_seconds": 213.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety and an irregular heartbeat are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.69,
      "end_seconds": 236.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.66,
      "end_seconds": 248.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.43,
      "end_seconds": 276.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 82, temp 36.8 degrees, BP is 128 over 82, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.42,
      "end_seconds": 280.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Is that alright, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.22,
      "end_seconds": 284.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.89,
      "end_seconds": 290.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.07,
      "end_seconds": 292.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.0,
      "end_seconds": 295.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.99,
      "end_seconds": 309.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft and your weight is stable on the scales."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.51,
      "end_seconds": 312.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Okay, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.65,
      "end_seconds": 332.0,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. So where does that leave us? My working impression is coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure. Iron deficiency is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.05,
      "end_seconds": 356.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Let's book coeliac antibodies to look into coeliac follow-up. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.79,
      "end_seconds": 360.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Oh, um, is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.5,
      "end_seconds": 381.43,
      "duration_seconds": 19.93,
      "text": "We should do a blood count for coeliac follow-up. Check labels carefully and use separate toasters and chopping boards. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. I'll want another look in twelve months. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.37,
      "end_seconds": 387.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Good, uh, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.99,
      "end_seconds": 390.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}